1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,200
A cyclic arbitrage normally reconciles three
inconsistent pools by executing three full swaps.

2
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:14,850
Even if a protocol reinjects the profit,
the EVM still pays for that full path.

3
00:00:14,850 --> 00:00:22,500
ARBFOLD asks whether cooperating v4 pools can
reach the same safe state more efficiently.

4
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:30,150
Path A performs the user swap, three arbitrage
swaps and profit reinjection.

5
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:39,600
Path B performs the same user swap, computes the
same cycle and moves backed ERC-6909 reserves.

6
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:48,150
Those reserves move directly between three
hook-owned pools.

7
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:58,050
At 100k: 544,187 gas versus 440,128.
ARBFOLD uses 19.12% less.

8
00:00:58,050 --> 00:01:05,250
At 25k, ARBFOLD uses 0.98% more gas.
The advantage is workload-dependent.

9
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:12,450
This is not three numbers changed in memory.

10
00:01:12,450 --> 00:01:20,550
The public demo uses the official v4 PoolManager
on Unichain Sepolia.

11
00:01:20,550 --> 00:01:28,200
All 28 deployment transactions and all three
demo transactions finalized successfully.

12
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:35,850
The post-deployment reserve, claim and backing
verifier passed.

13
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:43,500
Every virtual reserve must equal its
PoolManager ERC-6909 claim balance.

14
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:51,600
Token totals are conserved except for the same
capped solver reward.

15
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:59,250
No participating invariant may decrease.

16
00:01:59,250 --> 00:02:06,450
Canonical residual cyclic profit is zero.

17
00:02:06,450 --> 00:02:15,000
OpenZeppelin BaseCustomCurve computes and books
the user's output before the fold.

18
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:23,550
The fixed coordinator transfers backed claims
inside the same PoolManager unlock.

19
00:02:23,550 --> 00:02:32,100
Independent conservation and invariant guards
must accept the transition.

20
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:39,750
The router then settles every currency delta
atomically.

21
00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:47,850
The default suite contains 61 passing core tests.

22
00:02:47,850 --> 00:02:55,950
It covers six-path stateful invariants,
unauthorized calls and exact backing.

23
00:02:55,950 --> 00:03:03,600
It also covers slippage rollback and the frozen
five-size benchmark grid.

24
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:11,700
We preregistered a harder claim:
10% more LP net value.

25
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:18,450
It failed.

26
00:03:18,450 --> 00:03:26,550
Gas savings produced only 0.000287% LP-value
improvement in that frozen environment.

27
00:03:26,550 --> 00:03:34,650
The minimal harness measured 39.58%, the earlier
clean core 18.86%, and the delivered core 19.12%.

28
00:03:34,650 --> 00:03:42,750
We preserved every result instead of selecting
only the flattering one.

29
00:03:42,750 --> 00:03:50,400
Same outcome. Same user output.
Same solver reward.

30
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:58,500
At the canonical 100k workload,
19.12% less gas in the delivered core.

31
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:04,800
The advantage is workload-dependent.

32
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:12,000
ARBFOLD folds the cycle
instead of replaying it.
